Z||000000||JohnF||09-06-2001||11:28 AM||||I need to replace the rubber(?) under the male insert portion of forward portion of the glass.  These two insertable portions are held by Torx screws thru the glass which are practically impossible to get loose without tearing up the top "button" as this turns with teh insertable lower part.  Is it economically feasible to replace these rubber(?) portions?  Can I buy complete replacement parts?  If so, where?<P>Thanks<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=52558251&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Scott||09-06-2001||11:32 AM||||I believe what you want are the hinges.  You can still get them new from a dealer for ~$3 each.<BR>Scott ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||09-06-2001||12:39 PM||||Under parts.com, I find p/n 396480 as a roof vent hinge, hinge for about $3 and p/n 389481 roof vent hinge suppoprt for about $5.  Do I need both parts (twice for both sides of glass) or either or neither?||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||09-06-2001||05:54 PM||||Well, I got from my local Chevy dealer the 2 hinges, the rubber bushings, the top cap and two new screws for pretty cheap.  I found that it's basically impossible to unscrew them though... wasn't worth the effort. I only did one of the two (at least I started with the one that was rusting) because it took so long.  Of course, now, my sunroof creaks more than squeaks... I can't win.<P>But just check your local GM dealer... they'll show you a picture and you can pick out the parts.||||reg||1
